\section{Sections and subsections}{

When \code{.by} is supplied, the section is \emph{fanned out} into one subsection per
unique combination of the \code{.by} columns. Each subsection receives its own
filtered slice of the grid and its own title and description. Because
\code{title} and \code{description} are processed with \code{\link[glue:glue]{glue::glue()}}, they can
reference the \code{.by} columns to produce per-subsection labels — for example,
\code{title = "Results for {outcome}"} yields a distinct title per \code{outcome}.

Without \code{.by}, the section is a single unit with one title and description,
and glue interpolation of the \code{.by} columns does not apply (there are no
subsections to vary over).
